OctetRail is a Rust rewrite of dpkt, using dpkt as its Python API and behavior
reference. dpkt was created by Dug Song and maintained by its contributors.
Upstream: https://github.com/kbandla/dpkt
Published reference: https://pypi.org/project/dpkt/1.9.8/

The Rust parser/writer, test harness and synthetic fixtures are original project work.
The Python facades adapt dpkt's capture iteration, callback methods, timestamp
rounding, UniversalReader selection, link-layer offset data and the covered
Ethernet field/packing behavior, bounded protocol dispatch and IPv4 transport
checksum update semantics under its BSD license. dpkt's copyright and
license are retained in licenses/dpkt.txt.
Keep this notice and that license with source and binary distributions. No upstream endorsement is implied.

The TCP and UDP facades port dpkt's tcp and udp modules, including their
classes and constants, under the same retained upstream BSD license.

The IPv4 facade ports dpkt's ip module, including its class, protocol table
and constants, under the same retained upstream BSD license.

IPv6 base fields, checksum conventions and Python dispatch behavior use the
same pinned dpkt references and retained BSD attribution. The bounded Rust
extension framing, raw selector, opaque extension wrapper and synthetic fixtures
are original project work; extension-specific dpkt classes are not copied.

The explicit DNS facade uses dpkt 1.9.6 and 1.9.8 as behavior references for
header/question/record fields. The bounded Rust name and message algorithms,
structured serialization policy and independent synthetic fixtures are original
work, under the retained upstream BSD attribution and licensing above.

The HTTP facade follows the pinned dpkt field and rendering APIs under the
retained BSD attribution. Native framing and synthetic fixtures are original work.

The TLS reference module also credits: Portion Copyright 2012 Google Inc.
All rights reserved. Its API conventions use the same retained BSD attribution.
Native framing and synthetic fixtures are original work.

The Packet base class, hexdump and checksum helpers adapt dpkt's dpkt.py
under the same retained upstream BSD license.

The SSL and TLS facade and the cipher suite table in ssl_ciphersuites.py adapt
dpkt's ssl.py and ssl_ciphersuites.py under the same retained upstream BSD
license.

The Ethernet, LLC, STP and IPX facades adapt dpkt's ethernet.py, llc.py, stp.py
and ipx.py under the same retained upstream BSD license.

The ICMP and ICMPv6 modules adapt dpkt's icmp.py and icmp6.py, including their
constants, under the same retained upstream BSD license.
The GRE and PIM facades adapt dpkt's gre.py and pim.py under the same
retained upstream BSD license.

The IGMP and VRRP facades adapt dpkt's igmp.py and vrrp.py under the same
retained upstream BSD license.
The RADIUS, RTP, STUN and TPKT modules adapt dpkt's radius.py, rtp.py, stun.py
and tpkt.py, including their constants, under the same retained upstream BSD
The NTP, RIP, TFTP and HSRP modules adapt dpkt's ntp.py, rip.py, tftp.py and
hsrp.py, including their constants, under the same retained upstream BSD
license.
The CDP, DTP and EDP modules adapt dpkt's cdp.py, dtp.py and edp.py, including
their constants, under the same retained upstream BSD license.
The PPP and PPPoE facades adapt dpkt's ppp.py and pppoe.py under the same
retained upstream BSD license.
The AH and ESP facades adapt dpkt's ah.py and esp.py under the same retained
upstream BSD license.
The OSPF, SCTP and CRC-32C modules adapt dpkt's ospf.py, sctp.py and crc32c.py
under the same retained upstream BSD license.
The ARP module adapts dpkt's arp.py, including its constants, under the same
retained upstream BSD license.
The SLL, SLL2 and loopback facades adapt dpkt's sll.py, sll2.py and
loopback.py under the same retained upstream BSD license.
